1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,940
Nine a.m.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,600
For a Programmatic Solutions Consultant, the day starts with emails, Slack, invites, DSP exports, tickets and product updates. All at once.

3
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:21,860
Every answer is already in there: in a mail, a thread, an export.

4
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:25,640
But no one can see it all.

5
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:31,880
What if all of it flowed into one place?

6
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,680
So we built J.A.R.V.I.S.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
One AI brain, powered by Kiro, that turns all of it into a single place to work.

8
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:51,200
And it is one platform: mail, calendar, campaigns, clients, DSP news, documents and reporting, all wired to the same brain.

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:57,460
Every morning, a thirty-second briefing tells me where to start: mail, meetings, campaigns.

10
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:03,400
My inbox arrives already sorted. What concerns me comes first.

11
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:09,600
Every thread waiting on a reply resurfaces, and a follow-up is one click away.

12
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:19,600
It writes like me: it learned my style from my sent emails, and every draft is grounded in live data, tickets and docs.

13
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:28,200
I can always add a quick note in my own words, even in French, and it rewrites it cleanly into the email.

14
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,780
Every meeting is on my radar, unanswered invites flagged.

15
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:41,760
And a dedicated agent prepares each meeting the day before: context, numbers, talking points. I walk in ready.

16
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,380
Then, the campaigns. DSP exports feed the brain natively.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,600
The pacing map shows at a glance what's behind, what to watch, and what's on pace. I see under-delivery before my client does.

18
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:07,200
And numbers become actions: two percent delivered, forty-one thousand euros at risk, ends November fifteenth. That's now a task, with the next step.

19
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:14,720
When delivery breaks, troubleshooting is guided: TWIG, Waypoint, the twenty-four-hour window, and every SIM ticket tracked.

20
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:20,340
My whole portfolio is ranked by urgency.

21
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:32,640
One click, and I get the full client picture: risk, next step, latest emails, live campaigns and their curves. On one screen.

22
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:44,400
Seven hundred product updates? Kiro summarizes them, flags what needs action from me, and prepares a recap every Thursday. Slack is connected too, so nothing gets lost.

23
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:52,600
And because it knows everything, it produces. One sentence, and my PowerPoint for Thursday's team meeting is ready.

24
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:58,860
Even my weekly business review writes itself, from what actually happened this week.

25
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:05,200
All of this, in one platform. One place to work, one brain behind it.

26
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:11,800
I stay in control. Drafts land in Outlook, but nothing is ever sent on its own.

27
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:22,680
And it keeps learning: from every email I send, every document I create, every campaign result. Its answers and alerts get sharper every day.

28
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,120
Next: Salesforce, for sales and targets.

29
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:34,200
Then connected brains, sharing what they know, so the whole team moves together.

30
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,680
Stop searching. Start consulting.

31
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,060
This is J.A.R.V.I.S.
